  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Zigzag – first-time passes up the court and a one-timer",
  "description": "Three lines: A at their own goal line on the right, B along the right boards just short of the centre and C in the other half, a little left of the middle. A goalkeeper in the far goal. A passes to B and runs up the court. B plays it straight back and curves upwards. A plays a new first-time pass to B. Meanwhile C has run down in a curve and turned up towards the slot. B passes into the slot and C shoots first time.\n\nRotation: A to B, B to C and C to A. Also run it mirrored so both sides get trained.\n\nEasier variant: without C – after the second first-time pass B runs into the slot and shoots. Harder variant: C curves out towards the boards, receives, takes a few steps towards the slot and shoots, while B carries on, picks up a ball by line C and shoots as well. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "First-time passes should be firm and played in front of the player, so they keep their speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "C times the curve to reach the slot just as the pass arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time and hit the target – accuracy before power."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
